# /etc/tank-offsite/targets — what gets backed up off-site, and how often.
#
#   <path relative to /Volumes/tank>   <interval in days>
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored. Paths must be relative and must not
# contain "..". A syntax error refuses the whole run, because a table that does
# not parse cannot be trusted. A path that is merely MISSING takes out only its
# own target and alerts — the others still get backed up.
#
# After editing:  sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 644 targets.sample \
#                   /etc/tank-offsite/targets
# There is nothing secret in here, hence 644 rather than 600.

# Irreplaceable, edited maybe twice a year. A decade to accumulate.
my_media        30

# Small but the only dataset with real churn, so a coarser cadence than this
# loses work. Costs fractions of a cent at 1-2 GB.
documents        7

# Chosen folders inside `media`. The dataset as a whole is re-downloadable and
# deliberately has no offsite priority, which is why my_media was split off it
# in the first place — but individual folders in there can still matter, and
# this is how you say so without dragging in the other 447 GB.
#
# Add lines as you decide more folders are worth keeping. Each one is its own
# restic path, so `forget --group-by paths` gives it independent retention.
#
# media/concerts   30
# media/home-video 30
